    "source": "// v2 realms: two tenants, one key. Both stores provide `kv`; both apps\n// require it — and the composition links because provision disjointness\n// is per-(key, realm) (G2, paper Def. 43's \"disjointness within a realm\").\n// Each app also declares intercept metadata for its access (Def. 30),\n// consumed by the harness without touching provider or consumer.\n\nservice Kv {\n  fn get(k: Str) -> Opt[Str]\n  fn set(k: Str, v: Str)\n}\n\ncomponent TenantAStore provides kv: Kv {\n  isolate kv in realm(\"tenant_a\")\n  let store = effect Map.new() undo store.drop()\n  provide kv {\n    fn get(k) = store.get(k)\n    fn set(k, v) {\n      effect store.insert(k, v)\n      undo   store.remove(k)\n    }\n  }\n}\n\ncomponent TenantBStore provides kv: Kv {\n  isolate kv in realm(\"tenant_b\")\n  let store = effect Map.new() undo store.drop()\n  provide kv {\n    fn get(k) = store.get(k)\n    fn set(k, v) {\n      effect store.insert(k, v)\n      undo   store.remove(k)\n    }\n  }\n}\n\ncomponent TenantAApp requires kv: Kv {\n  isolate kv in realm(\"tenant_a\")\n  intercept kv with { quota: 5, tags: [\"tenant_a\"] }\n  effect kv.set(\"who\", \"alice\") undo kv.set(\"who\", \"\")\n}\n\ncomponent TenantBApp requires kv: Kv {\n  isolate kv in realm(\"tenant_b\")\n  intercept kv with { quota: 9, tags: [\"tenant_b\"] }\n  effect kv.set(\"who\", \"bob\") undo kv.set(\"who\", \"\")\n}\n"
