    "source": "// Time as a coeffect (roadmap item 57, docs/time-coeffect.md).\n//\n// A timer is a *revertible schedule*: `every`/`after` acquire a schedule whose\n// inverse is cancellation, derived teardown like any other effect. Unloading\n// this component provably cancels its timers — no orphaned interval outlives\n// the activation that armed them (the residue probe, item 18, would otherwise\n// catch the leak). The firing body runs at activation-time stratum with the\n// component's declared capabilities, so `emit log.write(...)` inside a timer is\n// audited (G4/G8) exactly like a top-level emission — a firing cannot smuggle a\n// boundary crossing the component did not declare. Under `revl test`/replay the\n// clock is a coeffect the harness provides, so each firing is a deterministic\n// timeline step rather than a wall-clock race.\n\nservice Log { emission fn write(msg: Str) }\n\ncomponent Heartbeat requires log: Log {\n  // a periodic timer: fires every 30 seconds for as long as the component lives\n  every 30s {\n    emit log.write(\"tick\")\n  }\n  // a one-shot delay: fires once, 5 minutes after activation\n  after 5m {\n    emit log.write(\"warmup done\")\n  }\n}\n"
